    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A chance encounter between two people whose destinies appear entwined soon sees them separated, then reunited accidentally, occasionally and unwittingly. This comic romantic fantasy is played with panache and no small amount of charm by Louis Garrel and Jasmine Trinca, with Moretti bringing his signature heart, wit and intelligence to the enterprise."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Adrian Wootton"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "With thanks to Cinecittà."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Content advice"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Contains scenes of nudity and sex."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Contains sexist attitudes and language."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "How to book"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Tickets start from £10 for all screenings and events in London, with concessions available for many screenings. Booking information and ticket prices .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Booking information and ticket prices",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=tickets-booking-information"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For non-Members we charge £1 per ticket for online and phone bookings, up to £3 per transaction. There’s no booking fee if you buy tickets at the box office."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you’re aged 16 to 25, sign up for free to BFI 25 and Under for a chance to get £6 tickets (without booking fees) to all screenings and events, subject to availability.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "BFI 25 and Under",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=25-and-under-lff"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Missed out?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "More tickets may become available for these screenings before and during the festival. Find out about extra ticket releases and standby queues .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Find out about extra ticket releases and standby queues",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=tickets-booking-information#extra-ticket-releases"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Our programmers recommend..."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/kettice-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Ketticè"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Following his debut Diciannove (LFF 2024), Giovanni Tortorici continues his collaboration with producer Luca Guadagnino on this vibrant coming-of-age story, set in early 2000s Palermo."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/common-story-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "A Common Story"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Anna Foglietta’s beautifully observed and impressively directed feature debut details the fractures that appear in a couple’s seemingly happy marriage."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/echo-chamber-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The Echo Chamber"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Andrea Pallaoro’s take on an unfilmed Bertolucci script is a frank portrait of a famous music producer whose life spirals dangerously out of control."
    }
  ]
